MINIMAL SIGNATURE CHANGE — keep a byte-identical no-skeptic path.

Keep reviewQualityBlockingReasons(result: ReviewResult): string[] EXACTLY as-is (cli.ts:5150-5163) — it stays the single source of truth for the pure reason list and is still called directly by the cosmetic site latestRepairReviewContext (cli.ts:5104). Do NOT change its body or signature; test (c) asserts the pure path is unchanged.

Add a NEW slice/store-aware wrapper that returns both the filtered reasons and the downgrade records:

  type GateDowngrade = {
    target: string;            // dimension name or concern text that was downgraded
    kind: "dimension" | "concern" | "status";
    fromSeverity: string;      // e.g. "failed/high" for a dimension, or "blocking" for a concern
    skepticVerdict: "refuted";
    reasoning: string;
    skepticActor: string;
    challengeEvidenceId: string;
  };

  function reviewQualityBlockingDecision(
    result: ReviewResult,
    ctx?: { store: SwarmStore; slice: SliceRecord },
  ): { reasons: string[]; downgrades: GateDowngrade[] } {
    const baseReasons = reviewQualityBlockingReasons(result);   // pure, unchanged
    if (!ctx) return { reasons: baseReasons, downgrades: [] };
    // 1) read latest finding_challenge; parse skepticResult; if absent/unparseable -> return base
    // 2) admissibility via listAgentRuns independence check; if inadmissible -> return base
    // 3) for each baseReason, if it maps (by dimension name; concern/status only via exact-string
    //    fallback) to a quality_dimension verdict that is "refuted" (and no matching "real") ->
    //    move it from reasons to downgrades
    // result.reasons is baseReasons minus downgraded; downgrades carries the records.
  }

Critically: when ctx is undefined OR there is no admissible independent finding_challenge, reviewQualityBlockingDecision returns { reasons: reviewQualityBlockingReasons(result), downgrades: [] } — byte-identical to today. The reasons array is constructed by filtering the SAME baseReasons array (preserving order), guaranteeing identical strings and ordering on the no-skeptic path.

CALL-SITE WIRING (no public signature changes; readLatestReviewGate and applyReviewOutcome already receive store+slice):
- readLatestReviewGate (cli.ts:4970): replace `const qualityBlockingReasons = reviewQualityBlockingReasons(parsed.data);` with `const { reasons: qualityBlockingReasons, downgrades } = reviewQualityBlockingDecision(parsed.data, { store, slice });`. The if(qualityBlockingReasons.length>0) block at 4971 is unchanged except it now operates on filtered reasons. readLatestReviewGate's RETURN type gains an optional `downgrades?: GateDowngrade[]` field so the verify command can record them (purely additive to the return shape; existing callers ignore the new field). Backstop branches at 4937/4945/4953/4962 are untouched and remain BEFORE 4970, so they are structurally immune.
- applyReviewOutcome (cli.ts:4691): route through the wrapper as `const { reasons: qualityBlockingReasons } = reviewQualityBlockingDecision(input.result, { store: input.store, slice: input.slice });` for consistency. NOTE: at review time the skeptic has not run yet (skeptic runs AFTER review), so in the live loop there is no finding_challenge for the latest review and this resolves to the pure path. Recording downgrades here is unnecessary/redundant; applyReviewOutcome keeps emitting only its existing escalation/event. (We could leave applyReviewOutcome on the pure 1-arg path; routing it through the wrapper is harmless because no skeptic evidence exists at that point. Choose the wrapper form for single-source-of-truth, but do NOT add downgrade recording here.)
- latestRepairReviewContext (cli.ts:5104): KEEP calling the pure reviewQualityBlockingReasons — cosmetic only.
